{
 "item": "14",
 "title": "Solver checks: operator checks, passive label, chain against one slab, step limits, cost",
 "status": "final (existing data)",
 "caption": "Solver checks of design note Sections 8 to 12, as they stand; every number is read from the data files under data/micropolar. Existing data of Stages 1 to 3, not rerun on thesis-ch5-rc2; the cards are one RTX 5090 and one RX 7900 XTX.\n\n(a) tab_14a_operator_checks (design note Sections 8 (T3, T4) and 10 (checks C and E); data in the tree since `micropolar-base-9-g278a557`). The micropolar operators on prescribed fields, one slab, 2-D at h = 5 dx unless said otherwise. Rigid rotation and a linear w_z with the regularization xi = 0: Theta alpha_z / c = 2 to 8.2e-07 and a / c = curl w to 1.4e-06 (largest relative error over the particles, lattice and jittered); with the default regularization 0.001 both are off by 8.9e-04 to 9.2e-04, the factor M (M + xi I)^-1. Relaxation of a uniform w (T4): the scheme's product is met to 4.6e-07 over 300 steps, and the difference to the exponential is the expected first-order one. Constant factors at h = 5 dx (check C, Richardson limits of three resolutions, orders 1.995 to 2.005): 0.9808 on xi in every direction, 0.9587 to 1.0029 on nu with the direction of the wave vector. These are the factors of the viscous form of that stage (Monaghan-Gingold) with EPS factor 0.0025; the thesis configuration uses the laplacian form with EPS factor 1e-6. 3-D operators at h = 4 dx (check E): exact to 1.5e-06.\n\n(b) tab_14b_passive_label (design note Section 10 (checks A and B); data in the tree since `micropolar-base-9-g278a557`). With c = 0 and xi = 0 the micro-rotation is a label that the solver must only carry: w_0 of every fluid particle derived from its global id, the n = 250 cavity started from the K = 1 state at t = 40.2, 1,500 steps, the state written and restarted, 1,500 more. 0 bitwise mismatches among the 63,001 fluid particles in each of the 10 runs (K = 1, 2 and 3, simple and adami walls, one card and the pair), 0 of the 11,528 wall particles changed; per run 4 defrags, one restart and 1,444 to 2,488 crossings of a cut in the chains. u, v and rho against Newtonian runs of the same two phases, largest sampled rms over the largest rms between two references (three references per run): 0.67 to 1.35 at K = 1 and 2, 0.94 to 2.02 at K = 3 (the largest on RTX 5090 (2 slabs) + RX 7900 XTX, simple walls); the floor of three references was too small once, 2.96 at K = 1 with simple walls, which is 1.02 when the comparison is repeated with ten references.\n\n(c) tab_14c_chain_against_one_slab (design note Sections 9 (T5), 10 (check D) and 11 (check D with ten runs); data in the tree since `micropolar-base-9-g278a557`, the ten-run set since `micropolar-base-13-g7e76dcb`). The micropolar cavity `micropolar_cavity_n250_re400` (n = 250, Re = 400, K = 3) as a chain of two slabs against one slab, on RTX 5090 + RX 7900 XTX (the pair) and with both slabs on the RTX 5090 (one card); extrema of the centre-line profiles of u, v (in U) and w (in U / L). From rest to t = 40.2 (1,340,000 steps, mean over the last 5 time units; in the .csv): relative differences to the first K = 1 run: the K = 1 repeat 6e-05 to 7e-04; K = 2 on the pair 3e-05 to 9e-04; K = 2 on one card 2e-05 to 3e-04. K = 2 agrees with K = 1 as well as K = 1 with its repeat, to three digits; four are not reached by either. Paired continuations from the K = 1 state at t = 40.2 (200,000 steps each, first time unit discarded, mean of the next five; cut at x = +0.0036 L from the vertical centre line): with five runs per group every quantity is within 2.5 K = 1 standard deviations. With 10 runs at K = 1, 10 at K = 2 on one card and the 5 on the pair (the table; differences of the means in standard errors of the difference): the minimum of w on the line next to the cut differs by +0.04 (one card) and -0.47 (pair); the largest offset of an extremum on one card is min v on the horizontal centre line, -2.9 (-4.6e-05 U; -0.4 on the pair), and on the pair min u on the vertical centre line, +2.3 (+5.4e-05 U; +1.0 on one card). Neither is established as a seam effect and neither is excluded: the offsets are in the fifth digit and the standard deviations are from five and ten runs. The L2 rows are biased low for K = 1 (each K = 1 run is part of the mean it is compared with). Per particle, 20 steps after a prescribed smooth state: the acceleration within 4 h of the cut differs from a K = 1 run by 1.5e-05 (K = 2 on one card) against 1.2e-05 to 1.3e-05 for a K = 1 repeat, and by 6.8e-05 to 8.6e-05 on the pair against 9.3e-05 to 1.2e-04 for K = 1 on the other card (relative rms, simple and adami walls).\n\n(d) tab_14d_step_limits (design note Section 12.2; data in the tree since `micropolar-base-15-g8cc60ea`). Explicit step limits by bisection on runs that stay intact or blow up: annulus with 101,768 particles (g = 50 dx), adami walls, EPS factor 1e-6, 2,000 steps at the acoustic step, the diffusivity raised until the run fails; h is the support radius (5 dx). Largest stable dt D / h^2: 0.0525 for the laplacian form of the viscous term (1.31 in dx^2), 0.0213 for the Monaghan-Gingold form, 0.0534 for the angular diffusion: the laplacian form allows a step 2.46 times larger. The limits are 0.96 and 0.94 of the forward-Euler bound of the lattice symbols. The cases use s = limit / 1.6: 0.0328 (laplacian), 0.0133 (Monaghan-Gingold), 0.0334 (angular).\n\n(e) tab_14e_cost (design note Section 12.9; data in the tree since `thesis-ch5-rc1`). Lid-driven cavity with 1,046,529 and 4,182,025 particles on one RTX 5090 (the rig's display card), K = 1 chain bench at depth 2, warm-up 1,000 steps, then 6,000 (1M) and 3,000 (4M) measured steps, trials interleaved; drift 0 in the 42 runs of the table. Steps trial by trial, 1M and 4M: paper to paper with adami walls 0.904 and 0.935; to the thesis configuration (form and EPS factor) 0.994 and 0.993; thesis to micropolar 0.771 and 0.774, so the micropolar terms cost 23 % of the throughput of the thesis configuration: 500 steps/s at 1M and 132 at 4M (523 and 552 M particle-steps/s). The trials of a row sit on two levels (paper row: 2.4 % apart at 1M, trials 1, 2, 4 on the lower one; at 4M trial 1 is 2.6 % low; cause not found), which is what the standard deviations of the rows show; the ratios hold within a trial. Traced runs: the force kernel takes 55.5 % (1M) and 54.6 % (4M) more with the micropolar terms; force and predict together are 98 % and 102 % of the added step time. Memory: +25 % per particle (369 to 461 bytes). K = 2 on RTX 5090 + RX 7900 XTX, 4M micropolar, weights 1.28 : 0.72: 191.2 steps/s, 0.934 +- 0.007 of the sum of the two K = 1 runs made at the same time (three trials), 1.44 times the RTX 5090 alone.",
